$MDESC::Type = "CTF_HamstersMaps";
$MDESC::Text = "<s3><f1>Mission Type: <f0> Capture the Flag" @
         "\n<f1>Author: <f0> Hamster_of_Doom!" @
	 "\n<f1>Questions, Comments, Pity: <f0> rvr279@home.com" @	
 	 "\n<f1>ICQ: <f0> 25400277 <f1>AIM: <f0> Rover v1" @ 
	 "\n<f1>Map Version: <f0> 3.1" @
	 "\n<f1>Updates: <f0> http://members.home.net/rvr279/hamster" @
	 "\n<f1>Map Type: <f0> Server-Side" @
	 "\n<f1>Planet: <f0> Larua" @
         "\n<f1>System: <f0> Mahkali" @
         "\n<f1>Gravity: <f0> Normal" @ 
	 "\n<f1>Weather: <f0> Clear" @
         "\n<f1>Time of Day: <f0> Midday" @ 
         "\n<f1>Date: <f0> Feburary 19th, 4025" @
         "\n<f1>Campaign: <f0> Brunt" @         
	 "\n<f1># of Captures to Victory: <f0> 6" @
	 "\n<f1># of Teams: <f0> 2" @
	 "\n<f1>Max # of Players: <f0> 30" @
"\n\n<f1>Briefing:<f0> Listen up soldiers! As you know, we were ultimately defeated in the battle of AirPower, near Kiam, and needed to retreat back here, to our main base at Opula Magnus, the capital city of Larura. We found that the this base has been under siege since January, and all communications were cut-off. The enemy has built a stronghold of their own to wage the battle from. They are trying to breach our base with a three-pronged attack: via the air, ground, and an underground tunnel they have constructed. We must defend our base at all costs, and stave off the enemy assault until reinforcements arrive. Attempt to gain and secure control of all three fronts. If you are successful in that endeavor, it may be possible to defeat the enemy at their own game! The fate of this system rests in your hands!\n\nFailure is not an option.\n\nDISMISSED!\n\n<f1>Tips:\n<f0>The more paths you control the better! Use teamwork and coordination to gain control of them all and keep them!\n\n<f1>Version History<f0>\nVers. 3.1\nUpdated contact info.\n\nVers. 3.0\nReplaced platforms from team bases to air base with ramp.\nReplaced inventory stations from air base with ammo stations.\n\nVers. 2.2\nUpdated (.dsc) description file.\nChanged cap limit from default to 6.\n\nVers. 2.1\nLowered height of central base to allow vehicles to land on it.\nMoved some of aerial base's rocket turrets to increase their effectiveness.\nRotated vehicle pads to face correct direction.\n\nVers. 2.0:\nRedid underground from scratch to reduce confusion.\nFixed mission description so it loads.\nFine-tuned placement of various items.\nAdded Repair Pack to Ground Capture Base.\nAdded Map Markers.\nFixed so objective switches have names.\n\n<f1>Thanks to:\n<f0>Shadow of Death and Tedaw for debuting my maps on their server!\nGerbil_of_Pain! for his suggestions on making the map play better.\nOmnipotent & others for their mapping tutorials.\nThe mapping community at large for inspiration, demonstration, and perspiration.\nAnd of course the team at Dynamix for Tribes!";